/// Read bytes into a caller-owned buffer through the stdin line contract.
///
/// `ins buffer` is an exclusive call-scope loan. The callee may fill the
/// existing allocation, but cannot retain it or return ownership. This keeps
/// repeated reads allocation-free and restores the caller's `erg` binding
/// when the call returns. The result is the exact number of bytes read, or a
/// typed `IoError`.
open verb read(ins buffer: Buffer) -> Result[Int, IoError] {
    /// `read` shares the canonical line reader and therefore has identical
    /// ownership, status, and end-of-stream semantics.
    return read_line(buffer: ins buffer);
}
